  "answer": "I found no earlier ticket that reports this problem: the Windows section's taskbar row in the new Shortcut Guide (0.100.x) cut off on the left and misaligned. The closest tickets are about different problems. PowerToys#48773 covers crashes and mispositioning of the new Shortcut Guide on Windows 10 when you select the Windows section, and PowerToys#9105 covers a jerky resize in the old guide when the taskbar is on the left. Please treat this as a new bug. Add your Windows version, display scaling (DPI), monitor setup, taskbar position and alignment (left or centered), and whether the taskbar auto-hides. Also attach a PowerToys bug report ZIP. That information should help the team reproduce the layout problem."
